.TH AVR\-GROUP 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group \- Build and manage the organization's group tree.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build and manage the organization's group tree.
.PP
Groups hold members, service tokens and vCPU limits. Organization members manage them while signed in (avr auth device-login or avr auth login); a scoped or service token cannot. What you may change depends on the groups you administer: `avr org governance` shows it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
create
Create a group below a parent group.
.TP
delete
Delete an empty group.
.TP
edit
Rename a group or change its label.
.TP
limit
Show, set and clear a group's vCPU limit.
.TP
list
List the organization's groups by path.
.TP
member
List, add and remove a group's members.
.TP
usage
Show the vCPU a group uses and the limits on its path.
.TP
view
Show a group's details and path.
